  "details": "Currently it is not possible to obtain unpurchased elements from previous months' VRChat Shop item bundles. For example, the magic potions from November.\n\nLikewise, the costs of these limited time items **can oft be too high for those on a budget to justify purchase all at once.** — Whilst the fear of missing out is a powerful marketing tactic, **the power of poverty is greater.**\n\nHowever, there is actually a very simple, and elegant solution to both of these problems:\n\n**Change the current pricing structure as follows:**\n\n1. Lower the item & bundle costs by about 50% **for an item or bundle's initial period.**\n\n2. Change items **to the current pricing scheme** after their initial period has lapsed.\n\n**This could have the following impacts:**\n\n1. Any item will be financially more accessible to VRChat supporters for their initial run, increasing the ability of obtaining them.\n\n2. **Fear of missing out will still be in play, as items would therefore experience roughly a 2x price hike for any item from a previous month.** — The shift would go from getting the item *at all* to *getting it on sale.* Sales work.\n\n3. This would also allow VRChat to run sales on older items, or even create new bundles which mix and match items from previous bundles.\n\n4. Poorly selling items could be discounted, thus giving the appearance of being cheaper than normal, whilst being more than what they sold for during their initial run.\n\n*…I really wanted those potions…*",
